{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"8cd23908931d33b0","name":"card_unit_the_tigers","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/OceaniaStorm/units/card_unit_the_tigers","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"THE TIGERS","text":"Gets +1+1 when you play a card that did not start in your deck.","flavorText":"\"The Tigers\" was the nickname of the Leicestershire Regiment, a British infantry regiment that served on several fronts during WWII. Its 1st Battalion was in the Far East when Japan entered the war, fighting in the Malayan Campaign starting in December 1941. After suffering heavy losses, it was amalgamated with the 2nd Battalion, East Surrey Regiment, to form the \"British Battalion\". This combined unit was later captured at the Fall of Singapore in February 1942, and its surviving men spent the rest of the war as Prisoners of War (POWs). Other Leicestershire battalions fought in North Africa, Italy, and Burma. The 2nd Battalion served at Sidi Barrani, Bardia, Crete, and Tobruk before moving to Ceylon and India, later joining the Chindits in the Burma Campaign. The 7th Battalion, raised after Dunkirk, was also sent to India and became one of the few non-Regular units selected for the Chindits. During Operation Thursday in 1944, it attacked Japanese rear areas and supply lines, but losses were so severe that the battalion was disbanded at the end of the year. ","faction":"Britain","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":4,"operationCost":1,"attack":3,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_the_tigers","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_the_tigers_title","SourceString":"THE TIGERS","LocalizedString":"THE TIGERS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":5,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_the_tigers_text","SourceString":"Gets +1+1 when you play a card that did not start in your deck.","LocalizedString":"Gets +1+1 when